## Ingredients

- 1.25 lb chicken breasts, defrosted
- 4 tbsp Mae Ploy green curry paste
- 1 can (400ml) full-fat coconut milk, not shaken
- 1 cup chicken broth
- 1 tsp brown sugar
- Salt, to taste
- 1 bell pepper, sliced
- 1 tbsp lime juice
- Cilantro or Thai basil, for serving

## Steps

1. Sauté: scoop the thick cream off the top of the coconut milk can into the pot, add curry paste, and stir about 2 minutes until fragrant.
2. Stir in broth and brown sugar, scraping the bottom clean. Lay chicken in the sauce, then pour the remaining coconut milk on top without stirring (helps avoid the burn warning).
3. Pressure cook on High, 8 minutes.
4. Natural release about 5 minutes, then quick release the rest.
5. Remove chicken and shred or slice. Switch to Sauté, add bell pepper, and simmer about 4 minutes until crisp-tender. Return chicken to the pot.
6. Stir in lime juice, taste and adjust salt, top with cilantro or Thai basil. Serve over jasmine rice.

